## Current permission policy

- Every person or organisation seeking to run or modify the software must apply for written permission.
- Academic researchers require individual written permission before running or modifying the software, including for research, teaching, evaluation or reproduction. Normal use of the hosted Informatics website does not require a separate source-software permission request under this policy.
- Approved organisations with annual revenue below USD 1,000,000 receive a fee-free licence for the scope stated in their written approval.
- For organisations with annual revenue of USD 1,000,000 or more, a nominal licence fee is negotiated in good faith and recorded in a written agreement before licensed use begins.
- Revenue assessment, the reporting period, group treatment, scope, duration, redistribution rights and the treatment of a later threshold crossing are recorded in the individual written agreement. Permission is not automatic at either revenue level. An application or fee discussion is not itself a grant of rights.

This is the current interim policy while the commercial roadmap and pricing are developed. Any later policy applies subject to existing agreements and rights; it does not automatically amend an agreement already granted.

